sqlgen: error: unknown option or missing value: --bogus
usage: sqlgen <command> [options]

commands:
  init      write a configuration with every default (sqlgen.json, or -c)
  model     load the schema and print its model as JSON
  check     load the schema and check it against the rules; writes nothing
  plan      check the schema, then print what would be generated as JSON
  report    print the model of an existing database as JSON, and check it
            (rule levels from -c when given, else the defaults)
  generate  check the schema, then write every target's files
  diff      what changed: --from <version> [--to <version>] between two patches,
            or --db <file> between a database and the scripts at its patch;
            exits 0 when nothing differs, 1 when something does, 2 on errors
  templates <language> <dir>
            write a language's built-in templates into dir, to copy and change

options:
  -c, --config <file>  configuration (default: sqlgen.json, written with every
                       default when it does not exist)
  -o, --output <file>  write to a file instead of standard output
      --db <file>      the database to report on or compare
      --from, --to <version>
                       the patches diff compares; --to defaults to the newest
      --json           diff: print the changes as JSON
      --key <key>      its encryption key (needs a build with CIPHER=1)
      --strict         treat rule warnings as errors
      --yes            clear output directories without asking
  -h, --help           this text
      --version        sqlgen and SQLite versions
